      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Segregation and linkage analyses were performed for adult height in a population of 200 Dutch families, each of which was ascertained through a proband with asthma. The best-fit model from the segregation analysis was a major recessive gene with a significant residual polygenic background. Models without a polygenic component were rejected. A genomewide scan was performed, and it confirmed previous linkage results for chromosomes 6q25 (LOD = 3.06, D6S2436), 9p1 (LOD = 2.09, D9S301), and 12q1 (LOD = 1.86, D12S375). Our results provide evidence that a combination of segregation and linkage approaches is valuable in understanding genetic determination of common complex traits."},
